## 1. Claim your Google Business Profile
It is free, and it is the first thing people see when they search for a local business.

## 2. One clear page per service
Google ranks pages, not websites. Give every main service its own page with a clear title.

## 3. Make it fast on mobile
Most visitors use a phone. Compress images and remove heavy plugins.

## 4. Write real titles and descriptions
Every page needs a unique title and a short description that makes people want to click.

## 5. Ask for reviews
Reviews build trust and help local rankings. Ask every happy customer.

## 6. Add your address and phone everywhere
Keep your name, address and phone number the same on every website.

## 7. Publish helpful articles
Answer the questions customers ask you every week. Each answer is a new way to be found.', '/demo/blog-seo.svg', 'SEO', '5 min read', '2026-09-12', 'published'),
  ('Why Your Website Loses Customers in 3 Seconds', 'why-website-loses-customers', 'Speed, clarity and trust decide whether a visitor stays or leaves. Here is how to fix all three.', 'Visitors decide in a few seconds whether your website is worth their time.

## Speed
If a page takes more than three seconds to load, many people simply leave. Optimise images and use modern hosting.

## Clarity
Your headline should say exactly what you do and who it is for. Clever slogans confuse people.

## Trust
Show real photos, reviews, client logos and clear contact details. People buy from businesses they trust.

- Test your site on a phone
- Read your headline out loud
- Ask a friend what you sell after five seconds', '/demo/blog-speed.svg', 'Web Design', '4 min read', '2026-08-28', 'published'),
  ('Social Media vs Website: Where Should You Invest?', 'social-media-vs-website', 'Social media brings attention, your website brings sales. How to make both work together.', 'Many businesses start on social media — and that is fine. But you do not own your followers.

## Social media is rented land
Algorithms change and reach drops. A post that reached thousands last year may reach a few hundred today.

## Your website is your shop
It works 24/7, shows up on Google and turns visitors into enquiries and sales.

## Use both together
Share useful content on social media and always point people back to your website to book, buy or contact you.', '/demo/blog-social.svg', 'Marketing', '3 min read', '2026-08-02', 'published');



